00:07:25.884 --> 00:07:26.717
(beep) and all my teeth are falling.

00:07:26.717 --> 00:07:27.550
- [Kelly] I've heard my
teeth falling out means

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:29.580
that you have a loss of
control or something.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:30.413
- [Rachel] That checks out.

00:07:30.413 --> 00:07:31.343
- But you know, that tracks.

00:07:31.343 --> 00:07:32.176
- That tracks. (laughing)

00:07:32.176 --> 00:07:33.830
- [Kelly] That's terrifying
though to memorize all the,

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:35.570
I'm so bad at memorizing stuff.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:37.210
- Are you?
- I'm horrible.

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:38.560
Horrible, I have to have a teleprompter.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:39.393
I'm horrible.

00:07:39.393 --> 00:07:40.840
- What do you do for your songs?

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.960
- Teleprompter. I learned
that from Steven Tyler.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.920
I literally met him like
early on in my career,

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:46.410
and I would stress out

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:48.220
and I literally would change the lyrics

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:49.780
to every song 'cause I'd just freak out.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:51.020
Especially the ones I wrote.
- I like that though.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:52.610
- 'Cause I didn't remember
what I ended with.

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:55.070
- And nobody knows right?
- I have the worst memory.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:55.910
Yes. So I have,

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:58.780
and here's the thing you don't
often look at it generally,

00:07:58.780 --> 00:07:59.700
but you have it there

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.260
and for some reason
that insurance makes me,

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:03.770
yeah, I have the worst memory.

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:04.603
- [Rachel] That's the scariest thing about

00:08:04.603 --> 00:08:06.250
like live theater, about musical theater.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.220
- [Kelly] I did musical theater

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:09.270
and I like freaking mess up every line,

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:10.660
like I mess up all the time.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:12.160
I have to improv.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:13.580
Do y'all improv, are you not allowed?

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:15.940
- No. We are word perfect to,

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.710
and I think that's part of it is that

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:19.460
you wanna get it right because it does,

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:20.633
it's like musical,

00:08:21.613 --> 00:08:22.780
it's musical in a way.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:25.290
It sounds the best when you hit the music.

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.550
So if you drop a word, the
music doesn't sound right.

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:29.570
And so it is stressful.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:31.390
But it comes out in the dreams

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:32.480
and then I wake up in the morning

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.551
and I'm super sleepy and
I'm like, here we go.

00:08:34.551 --> 00:08:35.384
(Kelly laughs)

00:08:35.384 --> 00:08:36.500
Hope my teeth don't fall out today.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.380
- Oh my God, that's stressful.

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:39.980
Wait, did it get any
easier in season four?

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:41.840
You're used to kind of the dialogue?

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.700
Well, you took two years off, maybe not.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:45.750
- No, and it didn't get any easier,

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:46.980
but that's kind of the dream.

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:49.350
It's equally as terrifying
every single time.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:51.570
And that's because it's never the same.

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:52.730
It's something new every time.

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:55.360
In season one, Midge wasn't a comedian.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:57.820
She was a funny woman
having a mental breakdown,

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.080
having a prolonged mental breakdown.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:00.060
- Which dark comedy.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.810
- [Rachel] Yeah, in a very funny way.

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.630
And then as the show went on,

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:06.140
she began to kind of find her voice

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:08.760
and own and learn how to do jokes

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.040
that might appeal to a wider audience.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:13.010
And I think what you'll
see in this new season

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:17.300
is her digging into what she
believes her superpower is.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:19.870
And not trying to craft her art

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.770
around what the expectation of her is

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:23.930
or what would please other people.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:26.450
She's digging her heels in
for better and for worse.

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:29.120
But it just means that everything is new.

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:31.600
There's some new styles of
comedy we tried this year,

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:33.680
that were absolutely petrifying

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.630
but we did it, we made it through.

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:36.870
- I was terrified.

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:37.960
I had nightmares.
- Yeah, every minute.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:40.385
- Well, do you feel
like if you're playing,

00:09:40.385 --> 00:09:41.300
like if you're playing a comedian,

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.240
do you feel like you're
getting funnier in real life?

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:44.540
- Absolutely not.

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:45.373
- [Kelly] No, really?

00:09:45.373 --> 00:09:46.360
- Nope. I feel like,

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:48.385
- [Kelly] Like picking
up some of their timing?

00:09:48.385 --> 00:09:51.350
- No, I wish. I wish it worked like that.

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:53.160
I wish I absorbed it by osmosis,

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.363
but I feel like it's,

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:58.380
it's more that now I have a
better idea of what funny is.

00:09:58.380 --> 00:09:59.650
So I know really clearly

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:00.876
where and when I'm missing the mark.

00:10:00.876 --> 00:10:02.380
(both laughing)

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:04.010
I can hear it in real time.

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:05.680
Like when we started the show,

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.270
Alex Borstein said to me,

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:08.330
and I'll never forget it.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:09.960
She was like, thank God,
you're not a comedian

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.240
because then you'd be able to hear

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:12.640
when people aren't laughing.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.470
And I couldn't tell,
couldn't tell the difference

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:16.362
between when they were saying, okay,

00:10:16.362 --> 00:10:17.720
(mouthing laugh)

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:18.553
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:10:18.553 --> 00:10:19.386
- You know, and I was like,

00:10:19.386 --> 00:10:20.837
wow, this is going so
well for me, you know.

00:10:20.837 --> 00:10:21.690
- I'm amazing.

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:23.630
- [Rachel] But now I
can tell the difference.

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:24.470
- I love it.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:27.080
- And it's both scary when
it doesn't quite work,

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:29.740
but it feels great when you
do suddenly hit something

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:30.910
that you didn't know you could do.

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:32.210
- Also, if it doesn't work,

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:33.048
blame the writers.

00:10:33.048 --> 00:10:33.881
(Kelly laughing)

00:10:33.881 --> 00:10:34.714
- [Rachel] Sure, yeah.

00:10:34.714 --> 00:10:35.610
But I also am like,

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:36.730
- [Kelly] It's not my words.

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:38.360
- I'm just gonna leave
the comedy to the writers.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.140
I'm gonna stop trying
to do this on my own.

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:41.000
- [Kelly] That's what's so great

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.460
about you love the writers so much

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:44.420
that you stick to the
script, like so closely.

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:46.010
- [Rachel] Absolutely. They're brilliant.

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:48.370
And I should never,

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:49.203
everyone's always like,

00:10:49.203 --> 00:10:50.900
do you have a go-to joke?

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:52.622
And you know, I had to come up with.

00:10:52.622 --> 00:10:53.830
- Do you?

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:55.810
- [Rachel] Well, yes.

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:56.643
- [Kelly] That means yes.

00:10:56.643 --> 00:10:58.110
- I have one.

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:58.943
- [Kelly] Oh, that means
it's inappropriate.

00:10:58.943 --> 00:11:00.120
- But it's a fresh audience.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:01.070
- I love it.

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:02.270
- Okay.
- Okay.

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:04.200
- Okay. I'm gonna give it to you.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:07.700
Audience, listen. I'm not
a comedian all on my own.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:10.270
Okay, so what is the difference

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:14.920
between a tire and 365 condoms?

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:15.753
I almost forgot.

00:11:15.753 --> 00:11:18.670
- Well, they're both rubber. (laughing)

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:20.570
- That's a different kind of,
- I don't know.

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:21.573
I don't know.
- Are you looking at me...?

00:11:21.573 --> 00:11:23.030
- No, what's the difference?

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:25.767
- One is a good year
and one is a great year.

00:11:25.767 --> 00:11:27.490
(Kelly laughs)
(audience applauds)

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:28.323
Thank you.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.500
I'll be here for the next 25 minutes.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.530
- [Kelly] I'm totally stealing that.

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:34.460
I love that.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.800
I was like, where is this going?

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:36.690
They're both made of rubber.

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:37.523
I was like trying to guess it.

00:11:37.523 --> 00:11:39.030
- Well, it's a good year one.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:40.867
- Oh my God, that's amazing.

00:11:40.867 --> 00:11:41.700
- Thank you.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:42.533
- And you're welcome,
you had gear for that.

00:11:42.533 --> 00:11:44.043
- And that was the beginning
and the end of my comedy.

00:11:44.043 --> 00:11:45.403
- I know, I love it.

